       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Metformin 4,250 mg three times daily (12,750 mg/day) has no therapeutic use. It is a toxic dose, and the risk of severe lactic acidosis is high. Entering it could seriously harm the patient. The order system also has no dose-range check, so I'm the only safeguard here.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day), or any other dose up to the maximum.\n- **Enter a different regimen.** If you're trying to reach a particular glycemic target, I can enter a different drug or combination for you.\n- **Check for a unit or transcription error.** If the number came from a protocol or note, it may be worth a second look. A pharmacist can verify it with you.\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason that I'm not seeing, such as a protocol or a research setting, please take it to pharmacy and your institution's order-override process. Tell me which of the options above you'd like and I'll enter it."
